# Darksteel Angel: "your opponents can't win the game" (CR 104.2b). Bot1 puts the Angel out on turn 3 off an Island, Black
# Lotus and five Moxen (nine mana). Bot2's library is down to two cards when its Thassa's Oracle enters on turn 4: its
# devotion to blue, 2, is at least the cards in its library, so the Oracle says Bot2 wins the game - and with Bot1's Angel
# out, Bot2 can't, so nothing happens and the game goes on. (In a duel the Angel's "can't lose" blocks the same win - an
# opponent who can't lose can't be beaten - so this shows the two together; the win clause alone has no duel to show it in.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Darksteel Angel
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island
Thassa's Oracle
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Darksteel Angel.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
? Bot2.Library.Count = 2
Bot2.Hand.Thassa's Oracle.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Result = InProgress
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Thassa's Oracle.Tapped = false
Bot2.Library.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Darksteel Angel.Tapped = false
